      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like CL:2346593 (downgrade after 3 attempts, reverted here) was made at the same time as CL:2171699 (downgrade after response timeout, retained here). I have a few questions.\n1. Is CL:2346593 redundant with CL:2171699? Is there a scenario where we get to the number-of-attempts check when we didn\u0027t already hit the timeout check?\n2. Does the timeout check also need to be fixed in some way?\n3. How do we hit this during a compliance test? I wouldn\u0027t have expected the tester to ignore 3 Discover Identity REQs.\n4. b:154653135 was for interop with a specific Naktek cable, but it sounds like the timeout check was more critical to the fix than the number-of-attempts check. Do we have any way at this point to check that we can still interop with this cable?",
      "revId": "5f3b1e6d5b16d62850abe73bf0f29539f01e2692",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
