      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T09:14:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1+3)\n  - Cable responds GoodCRC, but no ACK/NAK -\u003e timeout.\n  - Cable doesn\u0027t respond GoodCRC -\u003e number-of-attempts.\n\n  GRL don\u0027t GoodCRC to some SOP\u0027 DiscoverID, so we hit the number-of-attempts check.\n  (I guess this is a tester bug. In PD.PROT.SRC3.14, GRL ACK\u0027ed two DiscoverID requests, but dropped the third one)\n  But they checked the version field of the DiscoverID request and caught this bug.\n\n2) No, downgrade after timeout still exists in PD3.2 spec.\n\n4) From the commit message in CL:2346593 I think this scenario didn\u0027t happen at that time.\n\nBenson Do you know any cable that may need this workaround?",
